    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5196" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμετά-πειστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not to be moved by
				persuasion, inexorable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APo.</u>
				72b3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὑπὸ λόγου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Top.</u>
					130b16
				</span></i>
			; of necessity, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1015a32
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					222
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				1003
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<i>unchangeable, steadfast,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμμαχία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					37.20
				</span></i>
			.</div>
